
## Register the RetailZero API with your Auth0 tenant

1. Open the [Auth0 Dashboard](https://manage.auth0.com) and go to **Applications** > **APIs**.
1. Create a new API integration with the following settings:
    - **Name**: RetailZero API
    - **API Audience**: `https://retailzero-api`
    >Note: Your local Z-Assistant application's `.env` file already has `RETAILZERO_API_AUDIENCE=https://retailzero-api/` set.
    - All other settings can be kept as the default.




4. Select the **Permissions** tab and review the four scopes:
   - `read:catalog` — product catalog
   - `read:orders` — customer orders
   - `read:customer-profile` — private PII
   - `write:refunds` — process refunds

These scopes represent what the AI agent is allowed to do. The access token issued via token exchange will carry only the scopes that are requested and permitted.